>>secret?
> 
> Nearly Alpine play. If you can't carry it, it probably wasn't that
> important; leave it somewhere and collect it on the way back up. Best with
> combat wombats, who don't need spellbook collections. Don't plan on making
> stashes because then you'll have to return to them; just carry a
> reasonable mix of potions, scrolls, etc. You will probably have to live
> with being Burdened most of the time.

..looks like good advice for a fast (in RW) game but the OP was
originally asking for help on his first ascension. In that case I would
advocate making stashes, staying unencumbered, and paying more attention
to *in-game* time. Also avoid lurking and unnecessarily raising XP
level; always keep busy. After a few Dlvls at the latest, one should
start playing with a strategy in mind.

One of the first questions is whether to do mines(town|end) or sokoban
first. After this you get to know your character's strenghts and
weaknesses and can decide on what to do next. Don't let the game revert
to hack'n'slash after that, even if you're a combat-wombat. What
experienced players here refer to as hack'n'slash includes much more
"automatic" strategy and tactics than one might think..

